<title>ARGENTINA: Some rain forecast in Argentine crop zones.</title>
<headline>Some rain forecast in Argentine crop zones.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine maize, soybean and sunflower crops were enjoying more favorable weather Tuesday, with some rain forecast, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The weather is very good,&quot; a trader said. He added there may be some further slight wheat harvest delays if it rains in Buenos Aires, but they would not be significant.</p>
<p>The government's Meteorological Service forecast cloudy weather with the possibility of rain in most crop areas including southern Buenos Aires Tuesday. Weather Services Corp said highs would range from 70-88 F (21-31 C).</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
